                          "text": "SIR quality improvement standards: lung tumor ablation",
                          "href": "https://www.cirse.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/09/PIIS1051044321010861.pdf"
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "post",
      "kind": "post",
      "title": "Post-procedure",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "title": "Routine orders",
          "items": [
            "Notify MD/LIP - IR.",
            "CXR STAT and 3 hours post-procedure; order comments: 1 of 2 and 2 of 2.",
            "NPO until first CXR; clear liquids after first CXR if cleared by IR. After second CXR and IR clearance: outpatient, order regular diet and discharge if appropriate; inpatient, notify primary team diet is okay.",
            "Vital signs every 15 minutes x 4, then every 30 minutes x 2, then every 1 hour x 1.",
            "Tylenol 650 mg PRN.",
            "Toradol 15-30 mg IV x 1.",
            "If chest tube placement is indicated: place IR Chest Tube order and admit to inpatient."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "title": "Access care",
          "items": [
            "Wound care/treatment."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "title": "Anticoagulation to resume",
          "items": [
            "Warfarin: 24 hours.",
            "IV unfractionated heparin: 6-8 hours.",
            "Enoxaparin: 12 hours.",
            "DOACs: Typically 24 hours; confirm agent and renal function.",
            "Clopidogrel: 75 mg dose - 6 hours; 300-600 mg loading dose - 24 hours.",
            "Aspirin: 24 hours.",
            "Restart after hemostasis is confirmed; individualize timing for procedure-specific or patient-specific exceptions."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "title": "Discharge",
          "items": [
            "Discharge order with medication reconciliation - 3 hours; no discharge order if admitting.",
            "After visit summary: .IRAVSABLATIONLUNG."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "checklist",
          "title": "Follow up",
          "items": [
            "CT chest without contrast at 1 and 3 months; PET/CT at 6 months."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
